From: SAGA <saga@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] block/adios: self-activate topapp_deadline_bonus via in-kernel timer

Incremental on top of "adios" + "adios-topapp"
(0003-adios-topapp-deadline-bonus.patch) in that order.

Root cause of the earlier bootloop: the deadline bonus was classifying
requests by IO priority class (RT / high BE), on the assumption that
only the top-app cgroup would carry that on this device. That doesn't
hold during early boot -- some boot-time daemon(s) on the affected
device/ROM also run with an elevated ioprio for unrelated reasons, and
with the bonus active from kernel init, they got the same deadline
discount, which appears to have starved sequential mount/verification
IO badly enough to trip the boot watchdog. This is a boot-*timing*
problem, not a misclassification of who's-the-foreground-app -- so the
fix is to not be active during boot at all, regardless of who would
trip the classifier.

Two ways to gate that: wait for an Android userspace signal
(sys.boot_completed via init.rc), or self-time it entirely inside the
kernel. This patch does the latter, on request: no init.rc trigger, no
device-tree change, no separate kernel module -- the scheduler arms a
one-shot timer_list on its own queue attach and flips the bonus on by
itself topapp_activation_delay_ms later, the same way ADIOS already
self-manages its existing update_timer for the latency model. Nothing
outside this kernel patch is required for the feature to end up
enabled.

Note on the timer's epoch: it's armed inside adios_init_sched(), i.e.
relative to when ADIOS actually attaches to its queue -- not an
arbitrary "since kernel start" jiffies snapshot. On builds using
CONFIG_MQ_IOSCHED_ADIOS_DEFAULT, that attach happens at storage-queue
probe time, which is itself very early in kernel boot (well before
Android userspace/init even starts) -- so in practice this lands close
to "since kernel boot" anyway on such builds. It does NOT track
Android's sys.boot_completed and isn't meant to; that's the whole
point of doing this in-kernel.

Change:
- default_topapp_deadline_bonus now starts at 0 (disabled), same
  rationale as before, just enforced differently.
- New default_topapp_deadline_bonus_target (4ms) is the value the
  timer switches the live bonus to once it fires.
- New default_topapp_activation_delay_ms (90000, i.e. 90s) is how
  long after this scheduler attaches to its queue before that switch
  happens. 90s is a guess at "safely past first boot's mount/fsck/
  dex2oat window" on GKI-class devices, not a measurement on your
  specific hardware -- tune via sysfs, no rebuild needed, if boot
  takes noticeably longer or shorter on your device.
- topapp_activate_timer mirrors the existing update_timer exactly:
  timer_setup() at init, one mod_timer() to arm it, del_timer_sync()
  in adios_exit_sched() so there's no risk of the callback firing
  against a freed ad if the queue is torn down before the delay
  elapses.
- Both new values are exposed read/write via sysfs
  (topapp_deadline_bonus_target, topapp_activation_delay_ms), same
  SYSFS_ULL_DECL/AD_ATTR_RW pattern as every other ADIOS tunable, so
  you can re-tune or even force-activate early
  (write topapp_deadline_bonus directly, bypasses the timer entirely)
  without a rebuild.

This supersedes the previous boot-gate approach (userspace sysfs write
gated on sys.boot_completed via a separate .rc/.sh pair) -- that
approach is no longer needed and those files should not be used
alongside this patch.

Verified: applied cleanly (zero rejects, zero fuzz, zero offset) on
top of a freshly regenerated block/adios.c with 0003 applied first.

Signed-off-by: SAGA <saga@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/block/adios.c b/block/adios.c
+++ b/block/adios.c
@@ -115,7 +115,18 @@
 };
 
 // Latency targets for each operation type
-static u64 default_topapp_deadline_bonus = 4 * NSEC_PER_MSEC;
+/*
+ * Starts at 0 (disabled). There's no meaningful "top-app" this early,
+ * so activating immediately only ever risks catching boot-time
+ * daemons that happen to share an elevated ioprio (this is exactly
+ * what caused an earlier bootloop). Self-activates via
+ * topapp_activate_timer below, topapp_activation_delay_ms after this
+ * scheduler attaches to its queue -- fully in-kernel, no userspace
+ * signal, no init.rc, no module needed.
+ */
+static u64 default_topapp_deadline_bonus;
+static u64 default_topapp_deadline_bonus_target = 4 * NSEC_PER_MSEC;
+static u64 default_topapp_activation_delay_ms = 90000;
 static u64 default_latency_target[ADIOS_OPTYPES] = {
 	[ADIOS_READ]    =     2ULL * NSEC_PER_MSEC,
 	[ADIOS_WRITE]   =  2000ULL * NSEC_PER_MSEC,
@@ -249,6 +260,9 @@
 	u64 compliance_flags;
 	u64 latency_target[ADIOS_OPTYPES];
 	u64 topapp_deadline_bonus;
+	u64 topapp_deadline_bonus_target;
+	u64 topapp_activation_delay_ms;
+	struct timer_list topapp_activate_timer;
 	u32 batch_limit[ADIOS_OPTYPES];
 	u32 batch_actual_max_size[ADIOS_OPTYPES];
 	u32 batch_actual_max_total;
@@ -1426,6 +1440,19 @@
 		latency_model_update(ad, &ad->latency_model[optype]);
 }
 
+/*
+ * One-shot: fires topapp_activation_delay_ms after this scheduler was
+ * attached to its queue. Just flips the live bonus over to its
+ * target value; does not re-arm.
+ */
+static void topapp_activate_timer_callback(struct timer_list *t) {
+	struct adios_data *ad = from_timer(ad, t, topapp_activate_timer);
+
+	WRITE_ONCE(ad->topapp_deadline_bonus, ad->topapp_deadline_bonus_target);
+	pr_info("adios: topapp_deadline_bonus activated (%llu ns) after %llums\n",
+		ad->topapp_deadline_bonus_target, ad->topapp_activation_delay_ms);
+}
+
 // Handle the completion of a request
 static void adios_completed_request(struct request *rq, u64 now) {
 	struct adios_data *ad = rq->q->elevator->elevator_data;
@@ -1626,6 +1653,8 @@
 		ad->batch_limit[optype] = default_batch_limit[optype];
 	}
 	ad->topapp_deadline_bonus = default_topapp_deadline_bonus;
+	ad->topapp_deadline_bonus_target = default_topapp_deadline_bonus_target;
+	ad->topapp_activation_delay_ms = default_topapp_activation_delay_ms;
 
 	eq->elevator_data = ad;
 
@@ -1650,6 +1679,11 @@
 
 	timer_setup(&ad->update_timer, update_timer_callback, 0);
 
+	timer_setup(&ad->topapp_activate_timer, topapp_activate_timer_callback, 0);
+	if (ad->topapp_activation_delay_ms)
+		mod_timer(&ad->topapp_activate_timer,
+			jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies((unsigned int)ad->topapp_activation_delay_ms));
+
 	/* We dispatch from request queue wide instead of hw queue */
 	blk_queue_flag_set(QUEUE_FLAG_SQ_SCHED, q);
 
@@ -1688,6 +1722,7 @@
 	struct adios_data *ad = e->elevator_data;
 
 	del_timer_sync(&ad->update_timer);
+	del_timer_sync(&ad->topapp_activate_timer);
 
 	WARN_ON_ONCE(!list_empty(&ad->barrier_queue));
 	for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++)
@@ -1860,6 +1895,8 @@
 SYSFS_ULL_DECL(global_latency_window, 0, ULLONG_MAX)
 SYSFS_ULL_DECL(compliance_flags, 0, ULLONG_MAX)
 SYSFS_ULL_DECL(topapp_deadline_bonus, 0, NSEC_PER_SEC)
+SYSFS_ULL_DECL(topapp_deadline_bonus_target, 0, NSEC_PER_SEC)
+SYSFS_ULL_DECL(topapp_activation_delay_ms, 0, 600000ULL)
 
 #define SYSFS_INT_DECL(field, min_val, max_val) \
 static ssize_t adios_##field##_show( \
@@ -2051,6 +2088,8 @@
 
 	AD_ATTR_RW(read_priority),
 	AD_ATTR_RW(topapp_deadline_bonus),
+	AD_ATTR_RW(topapp_deadline_bonus_target),
+	AD_ATTR_RW(topapp_activation_delay_ms),
 
 	AD_ATTR_WO(reset_bq_stats),
 	AD_ATTR_WO(reset_lat_model),
